{% comment %}
  Renders a paper's abstract in an article, collapsed behind an "Abstract" toggle.

  The abstract is written for reviewers rather than general readers, so it
  stays out of the way of the article's own summary. The text is still in the
  page's HTML, so search engines index it.

  Parameters:
    text - required. The abstract, as plain text. Use single quotes inside it,
           since the parameter itself is wrapped in double quotes.
{% endcomment %}

<details class="post-abstract">
  <summary>Abstract</summary>
  <blockquote>
    <p>{{ include.text | strip }}</p>
  </blockquote>
</details>
